+To see the current configuration of your application, select an application
+and use the ``config`` command. The output is formatted as JSON. Keys
+containing ``SECRET``, ``PASSWORD``, ``TOKEN``, or ``KEY`` are matched
+case-insensitively and their values replaced with ``"***"``. Other values
+are preserved; values without a native JSON representation, such as timedeltas,
+are converted to strings. The application configuration is not modified.
+Only key names are inspected; review other values before sharing output. ::
+
+    $ flask --app hello config
     {
       "DATABASE_URL": "url",
       "SECRET_KEY": "***"
